WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.580
It's Friday, welcome to Tesla's short time,

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:04.880
daily episode 508.

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:06.560
I'm Patrick and Vancouver.

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:09.440
Today is June 12th, 2026.

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:12.200
Let's see how Tesla is heading into the weekend.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:16.240
Tesla Model Y just topped all foreign vehicle

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:18.160
registrations in Japan for May.

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:21.720
Model Y recorded the highest number of registrations

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.900
among any foreign brand vehicle in Japan during May.

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:28.120
The results highlights Tesla's continued expansion

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:31.840
in a market where domestic manufacturers have long dominated.

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:36.080
It also shows the Model Y maintaining strong demand

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.760
even as competitors introduce new electric crossovers.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:43.600
Next data point to watch is June registration figures

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:45.600
to confirm whether the lead holds.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:48.220
From real world sales momentum,

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:51.480
we move to the software layer that supports daily ownership.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:55.600
Tesla adds parking options display to navigation map.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:59.540
The navigation interface now shows available parking options

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:02.680
directly on the map as drivers approach their destination.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.780
The change reduces the need to switch screens

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:08.420
or rely on separate apps for spot selection.

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:11.600
It builds on earlier navigation refinements

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:13.340
that aim to keep the driver's attention

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:14.860
on the primary display.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:17.600
Watch for further map layer additions

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:19.380
in upcoming software releases.

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:24.720
An owner who puts 16,000 miles on a Model Y in six months

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:26.640
reported minimal battery degradation

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:29.400
despite heavy DC fast charger use.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:33.300
The capacity test result adds to real world data

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:36.560
on Model Y longevity under demanding conditions.

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:40.520
Fast charging frequency did not produce the capacity loss

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:42.100
some critics had predicted.

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:45.280
The same vehicle will be tracked over the next year

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:47.040
to see whether the trend continues.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:50.880
Continued tracking of the same vehicle over the next year

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.680
will show whether the trend holds.

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:57.220
Small UX wins like this lead into deeper infrastructure

00:01:57.220 --> 00:01:59.480
work happening behind the scenes at Tesla.

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:03.700
Tesla open sourced its TTP data center protocol.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.200
Tesla released the full specification

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:10.400
and a reference implementation of its Tesla transport protocol

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:14.900
on GitHub under the Tesla Motors slash TTPOE repository.

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:18.840
The company also joined the ultra ethernet consortium

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:21.620
to help standardize the protocol across the industry.

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:25.760
The move makes a custom high speed data center fabric

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:28.180
available for others to adopt or adapt.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:33.820
Inside dojo clusters, TTP operates exclusively at layer two

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:37.180
using standard ethernet switches and MAC addresses

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:38.920
instead of IP routers.

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:43.500
The design eliminates IP and UDP header processing overhead

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:45.900
for lower latency between training nodes.

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:49.380
It is optimized for a closed loop environment

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:51.460
where global routing is unnecessary.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:55.320
Future updates may reveal whether the same approach

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:58.400
scales to larger or more distributed installations.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:02.360
TSMC's COOP platform places optical engines

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:04.340
directly on the silicon package,

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:08.000
removing power and signal loss from final copper traces.

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:12.940
TTP then supplies the hardware level logic for packet flow,

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.440
state transitions, and rapid recovery.

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:19.380
The combination pairs a high speed physical layer

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:22.180
with a protocol built for silicon level speed.

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:26.420
Wash for any public benchmarks that quantify end-to-end gains

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:27.580
in training throughput.

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:31.260
The same drive for efficiency that shaped TTP

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:33.900
now appears in vehicle autonomy claims.

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:38.260
FSD supervise claims superhuman reaction times.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:41.580
Tesla posted new data showing reaction times

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:44.120
faster than human drivers in controlled tests.

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:47.440
The claim centers on measured response intervals

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:50.720
during edge-case scenarios rather than average driving.

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:54.500
It forms part of ongoing efforts to document performance

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.240
ahead of regulatory reviews.

00:03:56.980 --> 00:04:00.120
The latest software branch adds actually smart summon

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:04.320
alongside FSD supervised version 14.3.4.

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:08.380
The update is rolling out to vehicles already equipped

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:09.720
with the required hardware.

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:12.820
Owners will compare real world summon reliability

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:14.480
against previous versions.

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:17.900
Next milestone is the follow-on point release

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:19.540
expected later this month.

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:22.860
Elon Musk shared engineering through view notes

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:26.980
indicating the AI-6 platform targets major efficiency gains

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:28.120
over AI-5.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:31.960
The comments focus on inference performance per watt

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:33.240
rather than raw tops.

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:37.020
No public die size or process node details were released.

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:39.520
The chip remains an active development

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:41.840
with no announced vehicle integration date.

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:44.040
Future updates should clarify

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:46.920
whether the efficiency targets hold after tape out.

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:50.400
Autonomy progress sits alongside hardware scaling

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:51.620
needed to support it.

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:56.180
Tesla files for a 96-stall supercharger hub in California.

00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:00.720
Tesla submitted plans for a 96-stall supercharger site

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:04.140
in Willow's California along a busy highway corridor.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:07.300
The location would serve as a major charging hub

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:10.700
for north-south travel between the Bay Area and Oregon.

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:14.940
Construction scale exceeds most existing stations

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:18.260
and signals continued investment in high traffic corridors.

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:20.640
Permitting and build timelines

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:23.180
will determine when the site opens to drivers.

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:27.360
Charging expansion contrasts with regulatory friction

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:28.380
in other provinces.

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:31.840
Tesla lost its bid for fast track review

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:34.280
of Manitoba EV rebate rules.

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:37.260
A Manitoba court denied Tesla's request

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:39.860
for an expedited review of the province's

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:41.500
electric vehicle rebate rules.

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:44.800
The decision keeps the current eligibility criteria

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:48.040
in place while the full case proceeds on a normal timeline.

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:50.960
Tesla had argued the rules disadvantage

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:53.140
its vehicle's relative to other brands.

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:55.840
The outcome of the broader proceeding

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:57.820
will determine whether Tesla can sell

00:05:57.820 --> 00:06:00.260
into the incentive program on equal footing.

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:03.940
Several models from Lexus, Tesla, and Mercedes

00:06:03.940 --> 00:06:08.420
now sit at or near the $50,000 price point in the US market.

00:06:09.380 --> 00:06:12.340
The overlap places Tesla's offerings directly against

00:06:12.340 --> 00:06:15.780
established luxury electric crossovers and sedans.

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:18.840
Buyers gain more direct comparisons on range,

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:21.240
charging speed, and interior features

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:22.680
at this single price band.

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:25.300
Sales data over the next two quarters

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:28.360
will show whether the shared price point shifts market share.

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:33.340
Ferrari's loose concept joins six other high-end electric vehicles

00:06:33.340 --> 00:06:36.320
that do not include any Tesla models in the roundup.

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:40.580
The list emphasizes bespoke design, performance credentials,

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:43.400
and brand heritage over mass market volume.

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:45.940
It illustrates how traditional luxury

00:06:45.940 --> 00:06:48.420
markings are positioning their first EVs

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:50.360
against Tesla's broader portfolio.

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:53.480
Order books and initial customer deliveries

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:56.840
will reveal whether the differentiation resonates with buyers.

00:06:57.680 --> 00:07:00.780
Policy hurdles at home give way to competitive pressure

00:07:00.780 --> 00:07:02.080
from other EV makers.

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:07.600
Rivian CEO RJ Scaringe outlined two deliberate design choices

00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:11.080
that separate the upcoming R2 from the Model Y silhouette.

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:14.260
The differences focus on stance and proportion

00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:16.460
rather than shared platform elements.

00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:19.940
The comments come as Rivian prepares the R2

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:23.280
for a lower price segment or Tesla hold significant volume.

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:26.620
Production timing and final pricing will determine

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:29.460
how closely the vehicle's compete on dealer lots.

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:33.440
BMW's upcoming 800-volt IX-3

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:37.840
posted more than 500 miles of range during extreme condition testing.

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:42.120
The result exceeds current Model Y long range figures

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:43.880
under similar test parameters.

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:47.760
The architecture also supports faster charging rates

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:50.380
than Tesla's current 400-volt pack design.

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:53.880
Real-world owner data, once the vehicle launches,

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:57.600
will show whether the lab numbers translate to daily driving.

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:01.320
China's BYD demonstrated a charging system

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:04.240
capable of adding substantial range in five minutes

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:05.420
under lab conditions.

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:09.140
The test used the dedicated high-power architecture

00:08:09.140 --> 00:08:10.840
not yet deployed at scale.

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:14.280
Tesla's current V4 superchargers

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:16.680
top out at lower peak rates for most vehicles.

00:08:17.360 --> 00:08:19.620
The comparison highlights differing approaches

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:21.020
to charging time reduction.

00:08:21.740 --> 00:08:23.940
Real-world highway deployment numbers

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:26.000
will show whether the lab result

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:27.720
becomes a practical advantage.

00:08:28.580 --> 00:08:30.260
Real-world cost comparisons

00:08:30.260 --> 00:08:32.780
showed dramatically lower energy expenses

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:35.980
for Cybertruck owners versus comparable gas trucks.

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:39.320
The different stems from both electricity rates

00:08:39.320 --> 00:08:42.100
and the Cybertruck's efficiency at highway speeds.

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:44.720
No government incentives were factored

00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:45.940
into the published figures.

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:48.740
The gap widened further in regions

00:08:48.740 --> 00:08:50.160
with time-of-use pricing.

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:53.320
Fleet operators will likely track these numbers

00:08:53.320 --> 00:08:55.500
when evaluating total cost of ownership.

